| `audit_project.settings_tables` | list of strings | `["tool.pytest.ini_options"]` in keel and generated projects; absent, the same list, reported by the loader | a non-empty list of dotted TOML table names with no blank parts | keel's `scripts/audit_project.py`, through `scripts/config_loader.py` KEYS | Selects tables whose settings in the current template render are compared with DEST pyproject.toml. Each absent setting is a sorted warning in `drift`; present values are not compared. An empty or invalid list refuses with CONFIG (14). Generated manifests carry the value so their loaders stay silent; if absent, the loader writes `[using default] audit_project.settings_tables = ["tool.pytest.ini_options"]` to stderr. | proving work owed after update: the audit letter groups judge that | always |
